# Use the right tone

Write as someone who knows what the system can and cannot tell you. Be brisk but not curt. Say “you” where it helps the person.

<h2 id="wg-011">Match certainty to evidence</h2>

Say what was observed. Do not turn an estimate, an old reading or a request into a fact.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Alex is home. | Alex’s phone reported Home at 17:40. |
| The front door is locked. | The lock reports Locked. |
| The appliance is safe. | The socket reports Off. This does not confirm the appliance is safe to work on. |

Avoid “always”, “guaranteed”, “safe” and “real time” unless the device really promises them.

<h2 id="wg-012">Be calm without false reassurance</h2>

Give facts and a next step. Do not joke, blame the device or say “do not worry”.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Oops! Your pesky lamp is being stubborn. Just try again! | The lamp has not reported its new state. The request may still complete. Check the lamp before you try again. |
| Don’t worry, it’s probably fine. | The last reading was 9 minutes ago. |

Do not celebrate routine actions. “Light on” is enough. Use “we” only when it is clear who “we” is. Software is not a person watching the house.

<h2 id="wg-046">Do not blame or raise false alarms</h2>

Reserve alarm wording for real alarms. Do not blame the person or the device. Too many urgent messages teach people to ignore all of them.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| URGENT: You left the window open! | The bedroom window sensor reports Open. It has been open for 40 minutes. |
| Error! Error! Error! | Heating cannot reach the thermostat. It will keep the last schedule. |

<h2 id="wg-066">Treat presence as sensitive and uncertain</h2>

A tracker or sensor reports a device or movement, not a person. Say that, and do not show it on a shared screen unless the household chose to.

<%= example('wg-presence') %>

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Alex is out. House empty. | Alex’s phone last reported Away at 17:40. This does not confirm the house is empty. |
| Mum arrived home at 16:02. | Presence details hidden. (On a shared hallway display.) |
